cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Production and Control of Representations in Artificial Intelligence — Research II: A Conceptual Architecture, Authority Structure, Representation Lifecycle, and Research Protocol"
message: "If you use this research, data, or code, please cite as below."
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-04"
license: MIT
abstract: |
  Research II examines the structural relations through which
  representations are constituted before they reach a recipient,
  treating representation itself as the central analytical object
  rather than treating the model, the platform, or the user in
  isolation.

  The program specifies four foundational documents: a Conceptual
  Architecture (adopted, v0.2) distinguishing five functional units;
  an Authority Structure (pending, v0.1) distinguishing five authority
  types; a Representation Lifecycle (pending, v0.1) tracing six
  structural stages and five alternative paths; and a Research
  Questions document (pending, v0.1) formulating twenty questions
  across four families.

  No empirical work has been performed under this protocol. The
  literature review, methodological scope, and system selection remain
  to be determined following adoption of the four foundational
  documents. This manuscript presents an architecture and a research
  protocol, not findings.
keywords:
